    },
    {
      role: "application", time: 65,
      notes: `Two situations where this changes what we do.

When a report shows high-speed running, ask where the line is set, and whether it is the same for every position. Most GPS software lets you set position or individual lines.

When we plan speed work, use each athlete's own top speed. In one Gaelic football squad, players who touched more than 95 percent of their top speed in training had lower injury risk than those who topped out around 85 percent. Too little and too much both carried risk, and it is one squad. But the message fits what Athletic Performance already coaches: get close to top speed regularly, in sensible doses.`,
